{
  "tema": 9151,
  "slug": "jugar-tocar",
  "titulo": "Jugar vs tocar (to play)",
  "subtitulo": "«Juego fútbol y toco la guitarra.»",
  "foto": "t10.jpg",
  "regla": "English _play_ splits in two: jugar for games and sports (jugar fútbol, jugar al ajedrez), tocar for musical instruments and music (tocar la guitarra). Tocar also means _to touch_ and, in me toca, _it's my turn_.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Jugar** = play a **game or sport**. **Tocar** = play an **instrument** or a piece of music."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Pronoun",
            "jugar (u > ue)",
            "tocar"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "juego",
              "toco"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "juegas",
              "tocas"
            ],
            [
              "él / ella / usted",
              "juega",
              "toca"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "jugamos",
              "tocamos"
            ],
            [
              "ellos / ustedes",
              "juegan",
              "tocan"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With sports and games: **jugar al fútbol** or **jugar fútbol**. In Mexico you'll mostly hear it **without al**; both are correct."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With instruments: **tocar** + **el / la** + instrument, never **a**: **toco la batería**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Jugar** alone = _to play_ (kids, pets, having fun): **Los niños juegan en el parque**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Tocar** has other uses: _to touch_ (**No toques eso**) and _to be someone's turn_ (**Te toca**)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Los domingos ==juego== fútbol con mis primos.",
              "en": "On Sundays I play soccer with my cousins."
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi hermano ==toca== el bajo en una banda.",
              "en": "My brother plays bass in a band."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Juegas al== ajedrez?",
              "en": "Do you play chess?"
            },
            {
              "es": "==Tocamos== música norteña en las fiestas.",
              "en": "We play norteño music at parties."
            },
            {
              "es": "Los niños ==juegan== en la arena.",
              "en": "The kids are playing in the sand."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ella ==toca== el piano desde los seis años.",
              "en": "She has played the piano since she was six."
            },
            {
              "es": "No ==toques== las plantas, están recién regadas.",
              "en": "Don't touch the plants, they've just been watered."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ya jugaste tú; ahora me ==toca== a mí.",
              "en": "You already played; now it's my turn."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
